-- title:
--   Residue fields of C⊗_ℤO are algebraically closed of characteristic ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime. Let $C$ be a commutative local Artinian ring whose residue field is finite of characteristic $\ell$, and let $O$ be a commutative local ring whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $\ell$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_O = (\ell)$, and whose residue field $\mathrm{ResidueField}(O) = O/\mathfrak m_O$ is algebraically closed. Let $\mathfrak n$ be a maximal ideal of the tensor product $C \otimes_{\mathbb Z} O$. Then the residue field at $\mathfrak n$, `Ideal.ResidueField 𝔫`, is algebraically closed, and it has characteristic $\ell$ in the sense of `CharP`. Both assertions are delivered as a conjunction. Note that no finiteness or flatness hypothesis is imposed on $O$ beyond locality and the description of its maximal ideal; the finiteness used comes from $C$, which is automatically a finite ring under the stated hypotheses.
--
--   This is the statement that base change along $\mathbb Z \to O$ of a finite Artin local ring with residue characteristic $\ell$ has only algebraically closed residue fields of characteristic $\ell$ at its maximal ideals, the case of interest being $O$ a Witt-vector ring over $\overline{\mathbb F}_\ell$. It supplies the residue-field computation in [`IsArtinianRing.exists_faithfullyFlat_isLocalHom_isAlgClosed_residueField_of_finite_residueField`](thm.html#IsArtinianRing.exists_faithfullyFlat_isLocalHom_isAlgClosed_residueField_of_finite_residueField), which produces a faithfully flat local extension of a given Artin local ring with algebraically closed residue field.
